/-
# e-automorphisms are algebraic (Kourovka Notebook Problem 3.7)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.7 (V. G. Vilyatser): an automorphism `σ` of
a group `G` is called algebraic if, for any `g ∈ G`, the minimal `σ`-invariant subgroup of `G`
containing `g` is finitely generated. An automorphism `σ` of `G` is called an `e`-automorphism if,
for any `σ`-invariant subgroups `A` and `B`, where `A` is a proper subgroup of `B`, `A \ B` contains
an element `x` such that `[x, σ] ∈ B`. Is every `e`-automorphism algebraic?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Finiteness

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.EAutomorphismAlgebraicKourovka3Problem7Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 3.7 (V. G.
Vilyatser). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700161 (`KOU-3.7`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

With `A` a proper subgroup of `B` the printed `A \ B` is empty. The definitions are those of
Yagzhev's paper as stated in Yu. I. Merzlyakov's zbMATH review (Zbl 0692.20019): `σ` is algebraic if
for every `g` the minimal `σ`-admissible subgroup containing `g` is finitely generated, and an
`e`-automorphism if for all `σ`-admissible subgroups `A` and `B` with `A` a proper subgroup of `B`
some `x ∈ B \ A` has `x⁻¹ x^σ ∈ A`. This is also the `A ⊄ B` form of the definition in Kourovka
11.23 (some `x ∈ A \ B` has `[x, σ] ∈ B`). A `σ`-admissible subgroup is one mapped into itself,
`σ(A) ⊆ A` (an admissible subgroup of a group with operators, Encyclopedia of Mathematics, Operator
group), so the minimal admissible subgroup containing `g` is generated by `σⁿ(g)`, `n ≥ 0`.
-/

/-- `σ` is an `e`-automorphism: for any `σ`-invariant subgroups `A < B` (`σ(A) ⊆ A`,
`σ(B) ⊆ B`, `A` a proper subgroup of `B`), some `x ∈ B \ A` has `[x, σ] = x⁻¹ σ(x) ∈ A`. -/
def IsEAutomorphism {G : Type*} [Group G] (σ : MulAut G) : Prop :=
  ∀ A B : Subgroup G, (∀ x ∈ A, σ x ∈ A) → (∀ x ∈ B, σ x ∈ B) → A < B →
    ∃ x ∈ B, x ∉ A ∧ x⁻¹ * σ x ∈ A

/-- `σ` is algebraic: for every `g`, the smallest `σ`-invariant subgroup containing `g`, which is
generated by the elements `σⁿ(g)`, `n ≥ 0`, is finitely generated. -/
def IsAlgebraicAutomorphism {G : Type*} [Group G] (σ : MulAut G) : Prop :=
  ∀ g : G, (Subgroup.closure (Set.range fun n : ℕ => (σ ^ n) g)).FG

/-- Kourovka 3.7 (V. G. Vilyatser): every `e`-automorphism of a group is algebraic. -/
def eAutomorphismIsAlgebraic : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G] (σ : MulAut G), IsEAutomorphism σ → IsAlgebraicAutomorphism σ

/--
Resolved true: Yagzhev proves that every `e`-automorphism of a group is algebraic; the Kourovka
Archive answers 3.7 "Yes, it is". Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems
in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved
Problems, Problem 3.7 (V. G. Vilyatser); resolution: A. V. Yagzhev, A sufficient condition for a
group automorphism to be algebraic, Algebra and Logic 28 (1989), 83-85, main theorem (Yu. I.
Merzlyakov's zbMATH review, Zbl 0692.20019: every e-automorphism is algebraic); Kourovka Archive of
Solved Problems, Problem 3.7: Yes, it is, https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01980611.
-/
public theorem_wanted eAutomorphismIsAlgebraic_holds : eAutomorphismIsAlgebraic

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.EAutomorphismAlgebraicKourovka3Problem7Wanted
